# coding-problem-solutions
This repository contains solutions to various coding problems. Each problem is represented by a separate directory, and within each directory, you will find the problem statement, input/output examples, and the solution code.

## Problem Statement
Each problem directory contains a file named `problem_statement.md` that provides a detailed description of the problem. This file includes the problem description, input/output examples, and any additional information that may be helpful in understanding the problem.

## Solution Code
Within each problem directory, you will find a file named `solution.py` or `solution.java` (depending on the programming language used) that contains the solution code. The solution code is written in a programming language that is commonly used for solving coding problems, such as Python or Java.

## How to Use
To use this repository, you can clone it to your local machine using the following command:

```
git clone https://github.com/your-username/coding-problem-solutions.git
```

Replace `your-username` with your GitHub username.

Once you have cloned the repository, you can navigate to the directory of the problem you are interested in. For example, if you want to solve the problem in the `problem1` directory, you can navigate to that directory using the following command:

```
cd coding-problem-solutions/problem1
```

Within the problem directory, you can find the `problem_statement.md` file that provides the problem description and input/output examples. You can also find the `solution.py` or `solution.java` file that contains the solution code.

To run the solution code, you can use the appropriate command for your programming language. For example, if the solution code is written in Python, you can run it using the following command:

```
python solution.py
```

If the solution code is written in Java, you can compile and run it using the following commands:

```
javac solution.java
java Solution
```

Make sure to replace `Solution` with the actual class name of the solution code.

## Contributing
If you would like to contribute to this repository by adding your own solutions to coding problems, please follow these guidelines:

