    char_map = {}
    left = 0
    max_length = 0
    for right in range(len(s)):
        if s[right] in char_map and char_map[s[right]] >= left:
            left = char_map[s[right]] + 1
        char_map[s[right]] = right
        max_length = max(max_length, right - left + 1)
    return max_length
```

## Problem 4: Valid Parentheses
The fourth problem is about checking if a string of parentheses is valid. The solution is provided in C++ and Python.

### C++ Solution
```cpp
#include <string>
#include <stack>

bool isValid(std::string s) {
    std::stack<char> stack;
    for (char c : s) {
        if (c == '(' || c == '{' || c == '[') {
            stack.push(c);
        } else {
            if (stack.empty()) {
                return false;
            }
            char top = stack.top();
            stack.pop();
            if ((c == ')' && top != '(') || (c == '}' && top != '{') || (c == ']' && top != '[')) {
                return false;
            }
        }
