    const map = new Map();
    for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
        const complement = target - nums[i];
        if (map.has(complement)) {
            return [map.get(complement), i];
        }
        map.set(nums[i], i);
    }
    throw new Error("No two sum solution");
}
```

## Problem 2: Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters
This problem involves finding the length of the longest substring without repeating characters. The solution is provided in Java, Python, and JavaScript.

### Java Solution
```java
public int lengthOfLongestSubstring(String s) {
    int n = s.length();
    int maxLength = 0;
    int[] lastSeen = new int[128];
    for (int i = 0, j = 0; j < n; j++) {
        i = Math.max(i, lastSeen[s.charAt(j)]);
        maxLength = Math.max(maxLength, j - i + 1);
        lastSeen[s.charAt(j)] = j + 1;
    }
    return maxLength;
}
```

### Python Solution
